                <pb facs="0580" n="1234" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1234"/>

                <head>No. 7.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Earl of Derby to Mr. Comyn.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-12-18"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 18,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">le Ministre</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your letter of the 14th instant, inclosing a check on Messrs.
                    Huth &amp; Co., of this city, to my order, for the sum of £6,700, on account of
                    the claims of the families of the British subjects taken on board the Virginius
                    and executed at Santiago de Cuba in November, 1873.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DERBY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
